    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against soft pitching, headlined by our two elite OF plays: **Corbin Carroll** (82.08) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90). **Corbin Carroll** faces a favorable matchup against M\u00e1rquez, and despite a slight penalty for the pitcher\u2019s hold, his speed-driven upside remains paramount for our scarcity-focused build. **Seiya Suzuki** provides the day\u2019s most significant park-factor boost, surging to a 73.90 score thanks to a favorable environment and a pitcher with a slow delivery, which optimizes his stolen base potential. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (72.06) rounds out our top trio; his xwOBA profile and elite lineup position (1st) against Imai make him a primary engine for our Runs and SB production.\n\nIn terms of mid-range utility, **Kyle Karros** (61.17) is a shrewd start today. Beyond the favorable platoon advantage, the specific matchup against Wrobleski presents a key opportunity for **Kyle Karros** to exploit a slow delivery, which adds a 2% boost to his already strong projection. On the bench, the decision to sit **Isaac Paredes** (42.76) was the most difficult. While his park factor is enticing, he fell just short of our efficiency floor due to an unfavorable matchup against the talented Alvarez, whose elite skill neutralized the potential gains we look for in a starting option. We continue to prioritize volume and efficiency over name value, keeping **Austin Riley** (42.43) and **Max Muncy** (41.00) sidelined to protect our games-played caps for more advantageous splits later in the week.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk factors closely across the board, specifically regarding the \"below floor\" risks for our bottom-tier starters. **Mickey Moniak** (48.51) and **Zach McKinstry** (49.47) are active but represent the tail end of our viable output; both are facing unfavorable situational variables, including wind-in conditions for **Zach McKinstry** and a heavy platoon disadvantage for **Mickey Moniak**. While we expect **Gabriel Moreno** (66.50) to deliver a high-efficiency outing against M\u00e1rquez, owners should note that any last-minute lineup adjustments regarding batting order could further compress these scores. We are betting on the speed-weighted profiles of our OF corps to carry the day while we remain disciplined with our depth pieces.",
